  "variants": {
    "feed": "Decode and consume the entire source, but do not write; includes the common receipt-checksum work.",
    "indexed-bulk": "Multi-row INSERT, indexed path PRIMARY KEY WITHOUT ROWID, same full metadata.",
    "append-sql": "Multi-row INSERT into sequence INTEGER PRIMARY KEY table, no path index.",
    "binary": "Buffered framed binary journal; flush/fsync at completion.",
    "binary-periodic": "Same binary journal, additionally flushed/fsynced every 16,384 entries."
  },
  "methodology": [
    "Capture each variant in a fresh process; repeat all five variants three times, sequentially, using the same input stream and fresh output files.",
    "Every variant consumes and checksums all seven fields of all 1,000,001 receipts. No whole-manifest in-memory collection.",
    "SQLite statements insert 512 rows per execution, with 16,384 entries per durable transaction. Final checkpoint, connection close and parent-directory fsync are included in capture time.",
    "Binary output includes full path and all six 64-bit metadata values; fixed 1 MiB read/write buffers; durable completion included.",
    "Measure process peak RSS separately using /usr/bin/time. Report output size and observed SQLite main/WAL/shared-memory disk usage.",
    "Validate binary and append-SQL journals by streaming every receipt, comparing actual filesystem metadata, and counting the actual tree. No path index is built.",
    "Validate the indexed SQLite output using the previous indexed filesystem-validation method.",
    "All six final/periodically-synced binary outputs have exactly the same SHA-256 as the input metadata stream.",
    "Round-trip, partial SQL-batch, periodic-sync equivalence, truncation rejection and changed-filesystem tests pass, including under the Go race detector."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Writer-only timings include reading/decoding the metadata source; the feed control measures that common cost. Actual transfer integration overhead is not measured.",
    "This experiment assumes the transfer already supplies the required destination metadata. Additional filesystem metadata calls would add cost if an integration cannot reuse it.",
    "Source data was cached by the OS; this is local WSL storage, not a cold-cache or network-storage test.",
    "The first binary filesystem validation took 13.41 seconds; subsequent validations took 3.43 and 3.40 seconds. Metadata-cache state was not controlled.",
    "RSS excludes reclaimable kernel filesystem caches. SQLite cache_size is a target rather than a hard whole-process limit.",
    "Binary and append-SQL streaming validation assume unique receipt paths, guaranteed by this fixture. Production must guarantee that invariant.",
    "The prototype does not implement undo execution, crash/completion-marker protocol, retention, corruption recovery, or atomic validation against concurrent filesystem changes.",
    "Completion-only binary syncing does not give the same mid-transfer durability as periodic SQL commits. The periodic-binary variant measures the same 16,384-entry flush cadence.",
    "An append-only journal lacks indexed path lookup. Reverse/action ordering and concurrency protections need separate production design."
  ],
